OL,3,ACriminals who skip sentencing will face
OL,4,Asolitary confinement or lose social
OL,5,Avisits
OL,6,
OL,7,FJudges in England and Wales will be
OL,8,Fgiven stronger powers to block prison
OL,9,Fvisits and keep offenders in their
OL,10,Fcells for weeks on end if they refuse
OL,11,Fto face their victims' families during
OL,12,Fsentencing.
OL,14,FThe tougher sanctions, due to come into
OL,15,Feffect next year, build on an existing
OL,16,Flaw that orders criminals to attend
OL,17,Fsentencing or face being fined or
OL,18,Fjailed for another two years for
OL,19,Fcontempt of court.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
